# SuccessionAI

Inference-time organizational knowledge auditing and workforce readiness evaluation.

## What This Is

A multi-agent reasoning system that audits an organization's collective knowledge,
identifies undocumented expertise, interviews the people who hold it, and converts
that expertise into hiring and onboarding intelligence.

## Core Flow

1. Detect knowledge risk (who holds critical undocumented knowledge).
2. Run multi-agent audit (5 agents debate, verify, challenge in parallel).
3. Conduct targeted exit interview (gap-driven, investigator tone).
4. Generate hiring spec from confirmed knowledge gaps.
5. Evaluate candidates via gap analysis + adaptability assessment.

## Architecture

- One LLM endpoint (OpenAI-compatible). Claude in dev, vLLM on GPU day.
- Five agents: Evidence, Expertise, Risk, Skeptic, Question.
- Agents debate in rounds — findings slide in, disagreements highlighted.
- Tavus for video interviewer. No custom avatar infra.
- JSON data files (no real Jira/GitHub integration for demo).

## Read .cursor/SPEC.md for full implementation details.

## Coding Rules

- Use strict TypeScript and descriptive names.
- Follow existing Next.js App Router patterns.
- Validate API input with Zod.
- All agents call `lib/llm.ts` — never call Claude directly.
- Agent outputs are structured JSON (Zod-validated).
- Show confidence levels and evidence citations on every claim.
- Never claim omniscience — expose uncertainty.
- Never say "best candidate" — say "gap coverage" (factual).
- Use shadcn/ui components. Light mode only.
- Design: Linear + Vercel + Stripe aesthetic. Minimal, professional.
- Keep the demo path fast, stable, and easy to present live.
- Run `npm run build` after meaningful changes.

## Do NOT Build

- Digital twin / fine-tuning / LoRA
- GRPO / RL training
- Dark mode
- Complex video avatar (LivePortrait, voice cloning)
- Full Jira/GitHub OAuth integration
- Admin settings / user accounts
- Knowledge graph 3D visualization (optional, cut if time-tight)
